1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,083
A ruler tells you how long a pencil is.

2
00:00:03,083 --> 00:00:04,217
Not its colour.

3
00:00:04,617 --> 00:00:07,439
A thermometer reads
temperature, not your mood.

4
00:00:07,439 --> 00:00:08,977
Every tool has a limit.

5
00:00:09,427 --> 00:00:13,173
Last time, Aarav used dimensions
on the corridor swing.

6
00:00:13,173 --> 00:00:15,561
Its time depends on length and g.

7
00:00:15,911 --> 00:00:19,463
But his textbook says T
equals two pi, root l by g.

8
00:00:19,463 --> 00:00:21,690
Where did that two pi come from?

9
00:00:22,190 --> 00:00:24,017
His method could not find it.

10
00:00:24,017 --> 00:00:26,802
Today, see why, and
what else it cannot do.

11
00:00:27,452 --> 00:00:28,643
Quick reminder.

12
00:00:28,643 --> 00:00:31,090
What does dimensional analysis use?

13
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,491
It looks only at dimensions.

14
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,773
Mass M, length L and time T.

15
00:00:36,123 --> 00:00:40,249
It can check a formula, convert
units, and even guess a formula.

16
00:00:40,599 --> 00:00:42,742
But it never looks at plain numbers.

17
00:00:42,742 --> 00:00:44,035
That is the trouble.

18
00:00:44,685 --> 00:00:48,011
Let's test a real pendulum
on our measuring bench.

19
00:00:48,361 --> 00:00:50,230
A string half a metre long.

20
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:52,976
One swing takes one
point four two seconds.

21
00:00:53,376 --> 00:00:54,795
Make it one metre.

22
00:00:54,795 --> 00:00:57,419
Now one swing takes about two seconds.

23
00:00:57,819 --> 00:00:59,205
Make it two metres.

24
00:00:59,205 --> 00:01:01,129
Two point eight four seconds.

25
00:01:01,529 --> 00:01:04,153
Now divide the time by root l over g.

26
00:01:04,153 --> 00:01:06,916
Every time, we get six point two eight.

27
00:01:07,316 --> 00:01:08,490
That is two pi.

28
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:12,786
All three points sit on one straight
line, and its slope is two pi.

29
00:01:13,436 --> 00:01:15,118
Let's freeze one swing.

30
00:01:15,118 --> 00:01:16,143
Slow motion.

31
00:01:16,493 --> 00:01:18,981
At the bottom, the bob moves fastest.

32
00:01:18,981 --> 00:01:21,174
Gravity pulls down the whole time.

33
00:01:21,174 --> 00:01:23,330
The real swing knows the two pi.

34
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:27,519
Now let dimensional analysis
try, one step at a time.

35
00:01:27,869 --> 00:01:28,769
Step one.

36
00:01:28,724 --> 00:01:33,761
Guess that T equals k, times l
to the a, m to the b, g to the c.

37
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:35,411
Step two.

38
00:01:35,326 --> 00:01:36,798
Write the dimensions.

39
00:01:36,798 --> 00:01:41,354
L to the a, M to the b, and
LT to the minus two, to the c.

40
00:01:42,104 --> 00:01:43,081
Step three.

41
00:01:43,081 --> 00:01:44,440
Match the powers.

42
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:46,351
Mass gives b equals zero.

43
00:01:46,351 --> 00:01:48,815
Time gives c equals minus a half.

44
00:01:48,815 --> 00:01:51,002
Length gives a equals a half.

45
00:01:51,752 --> 00:01:52,694
Step four.

46
00:01:52,694 --> 00:01:55,163
So T equals k, root l over g.

47
00:01:55,163 --> 00:01:57,166
And here the method stops.

48
00:01:57,916 --> 00:01:59,172
Why does it stop?

49
00:01:59,172 --> 00:02:00,371
Follow the links.

50
00:02:00,721 --> 00:02:02,210
k is a plain number.

51
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:05,583
A plain number has no mass,
no length and no time.

52
00:02:05,983 --> 00:02:10,593
So its dimension is M to the zero,
L to the zero, T to the zero.

53
00:02:10,993 --> 00:02:14,355
Multiply by two pi, by
ten, or by one half.

54
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:16,456
The dimensions do not change.

55
00:02:16,856 --> 00:02:19,075
So the method cannot tell them apart.

56
00:02:19,075 --> 00:02:22,245
The two pi must come from
experiment, or from theory.

57
00:02:22,895 --> 00:02:24,501
That is limitation one.

58
00:02:24,501 --> 00:02:26,606
It cannot find number constants.

59
00:02:27,106 --> 00:02:28,447
Limitation two.

60
00:02:28,447 --> 00:02:30,843
Two formulas, side by side.

61
00:02:31,243 --> 00:02:34,831
On the left, s equals u
t, plus half a t squared.

62
00:02:34,831 --> 00:02:36,417
This is the real one.

63
00:02:36,817 --> 00:02:40,351
On the right, s equals u
t, plus two a t squared.

64
00:02:40,351 --> 00:02:42,313
A two has replaced the half.

65
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:44,151
Pause and think.

66
00:02:44,151 --> 00:02:46,730
Is the right one dimensionally correct?

67
00:02:46,730 --> 00:02:47,666
Yes or no?

68
00:02:50,866 --> 00:02:51,766
Yes!

69
00:02:51,374 --> 00:02:53,068
Every term is a length.

70
00:02:53,068 --> 00:02:55,220
But the formula is still wrong.

71
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,262
Dimensions cannot see the two.

72
00:02:57,912 --> 00:02:59,412
Here is a sneakier case.

73
00:02:59,412 --> 00:03:01,915
Work, and the turning
effect called torque.

74
00:03:02,315 --> 00:03:04,566
Work is force times distance moved.

75
00:03:04,566 --> 00:03:06,970
Torque is force times the arm length.

76
00:03:07,370 --> 00:03:10,318
Both give ML squared T to the minus two.

77
00:03:10,318 --> 00:03:13,023
Can dimensional analysis tell them apart?

78
00:03:13,023 --> 00:03:14,324
Pause and decide.

79
00:03:17,524 --> 00:03:18,424
No!

80
00:03:17,988 --> 00:03:20,501
Same dimensions, different quantities.

81
00:03:20,501 --> 00:03:23,035
Matching never proves a formula right.

82
00:03:23,685 --> 00:03:24,970
Limitation three.

83
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:30,196
It only builds products of powers, like
l to the half, times g to the minus

84
00:03:30,196 --> 00:03:31,096
half.

85
00:03:31,136 --> 00:03:35,024
So it cannot build a sum, like
u t plus half a t squared.

86
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:38,634
And it cannot build
sine, log or e to the x.

87
00:03:38,634 --> 00:03:40,844
Those need a pure number inside.

88
00:03:41,444 --> 00:03:42,702
Limitation four.

89
00:03:42,702 --> 00:03:46,230
In mechanics, we have only
three base dimensions.

90
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:47,457
M, L and T.

91
00:03:47,807 --> 00:03:49,811
That gives only three equations.

92
00:03:49,811 --> 00:03:52,972
With four or more unknowns,
the method gets stuck.

93
00:03:53,622 --> 00:03:54,687
Remember this.

94
00:03:54,687 --> 00:03:56,977
Wrong dimensions mean surely wrong.

95
00:03:56,977 --> 00:03:59,526
Right dimensions mean only maybe right.

96
00:04:00,226 --> 00:04:01,961
Now, one worked example.

97
00:04:02,311 --> 00:04:07,539
A swing two point four five metres long
takes three point one four seconds.

98
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:08,439
Find k.

99
00:04:08,816 --> 00:04:14,952
From T equals k root l over g, k
equals T, divided by root l over g.

100
00:04:15,702 --> 00:04:19,505
l over g is two point four
five, over nine point eight.

101
00:04:19,505 --> 00:04:21,507
That is zero point two five.

102
00:04:22,257 --> 00:04:26,760
The square root of zero point two
five is zero point five seconds.

103
00:04:27,510 --> 00:04:31,034
So k is three point one
four over zero point five.

104
00:04:31,034 --> 00:04:32,574
Six point two eight.

105
00:04:32,574 --> 00:04:34,641
Two pi, found by measuring.

106
00:04:35,291 --> 00:04:36,756
Now, the exam trap.

107
00:04:37,106 --> 00:04:41,582
Many students think: the dimensions
match, so the formula must be correct.

108
00:04:41,932 --> 00:04:42,832
Wrong.

109
00:04:42,526 --> 00:04:45,624
Matching dimensions only
means it might be right.

110
00:04:45,624 --> 00:04:48,079
A wrong number can still hide inside.

111
00:04:48,729 --> 00:04:50,100
Where is this asked?

112
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,554
As statement questions.

113
00:04:51,554 --> 00:04:54,730
Which formula can it derive,
and which can it not?

114
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:56,552
Exam level now.

115
00:04:56,552 --> 00:05:01,700
Which of these could dimensional analysis
alone derive, apart from a constant?

116
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:02,975
Pause and solve.

117
00:05:08,375 --> 00:05:09,773
The answer is B.

118
00:05:09,773 --> 00:05:12,505
The pendulum period, root l over g.

119
00:05:13,005 --> 00:05:14,911
A is a sum of two terms.

120
00:05:14,911 --> 00:05:16,481
C has an exponential.

121
00:05:16,481 --> 00:05:17,644
D has a sine.

122
00:05:18,144 --> 00:05:20,250
Only B is a product of powers.

123
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:23,239
Even there, the two pi
comes from experiment.

124
00:05:23,839 --> 00:05:25,298
Here is your recap.

125
00:05:25,298 --> 00:05:26,797
Screenshot this card.

126
00:05:29,997 --> 00:05:32,996
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

127
00:05:33,396 --> 00:05:34,296
One.

128
00:05:33,936 --> 00:05:38,367
Why can the method not find the
two pi in the pendulum formula?

129
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:40,167
Two.

130
00:05:39,745 --> 00:05:42,294
Work and torque have the same dimensions.

131
00:05:42,294 --> 00:05:43,933
What does that tell you?

132
00:05:44,833 --> 00:05:45,733
Three.

133
00:05:45,496 --> 00:05:50,438
Why can the method not derive s
equals u t, plus half a t squared?

134
00:05:51,538 --> 00:05:56,772
Next time: is the extra zero in two
fifty point zero grams worth anything?

135
00:05:56,772 --> 00:05:59,073
Find out in significant figures.
